name o4-05-entry-5nm-1
timeout 300

# CAMPAIGN O4, SORTIE 5 OF 10 — INSIDE THE CLAIM. doc/campaigns/o4-gaf-mig29g-dact.md mission 5.
# This file is o4-04-entry-10nm.fbm with the two entry longitudes moved inward to 5.00 nm and NOTHING
# else changed but the callsigns. The callsigns are fresh because the campaign carries `stores`, and a
# controlled variant that inherits its control's expenditure is not a control.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: what does the module hook that decides whether a shot is OFFERED do to the
# outcome when the entry is halved? The two hooks are not the same size and neither is mission data —
# they are what the two aircraft ARE:
#   R-73   +-75 deg seeker gimbal [DOC], cued by the Shchel-3UM helmet sight to +-60 deg [T4/hook],
#          Raero 20,000 m
#   AIM-9M +-30 deg, no helmet sight anywhere in the western inventory until 2003 [T4],
#          Raero 12,000 m
# [MESS, o4-04] at a 10 nm entry that difference is worth 11.0 s and 5.8 km of first shot: the MiG's
# BFM_SHOT is accepted at t=1.5 with rangeM 17,796 and cueDeg 60, the F-16's not until t=12.5 at
# rangeM 11,963 with cueDeg 30 — because 17.8 km is inside the R-73's Raero and outside the AIM-9's.
# At 5 nm BOTH rounds are inside their envelope from the first tick, so the hook that decided sortie 4
# cannot decide this one. What is left is the endgame: 9.4 kg of AIM-9M warhead against 7.4 kg of R-73,
# a 2.32 m kill radius against 2.08 m, and whichever arrival geometry the two jets fly into
# (doc/duels.md D2, row 8, row 9).
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-29): exit 1, A TRADE. Both shots are accepted inside 0.4 s of each other (fulcrum
# t=1.5 at 8,533 m, viper t=1.9 at 8,338 m) because both rounds are in envelope from the first tick, and
# both arrive: AIM-9 1.63 m -> KILL at t=11.8, R-73 2.00 m -> KILL at t=11.9. 0.1 s apart. exit 1 is the
# verdict layer refusing to invent a winner (doc/missions/verdict.md, "a trade"). Against o4-04's MiG win
# that is the sweep's middle point, and it says the ten-mile edge is an ENVELOPE edge: halve the entry and
# the envelope stops discriminating.
#
# READING RULE: the verdict is the TELEMETRY, not the exit code. Read the BFM_SHOT lines (t, rangeM,
# cueDeg, accepted), then the DETONATION lines (missM against fuzeM), then eng_shots. Read this file
# ONLY beside o4-04: a single entry range is a point, and the campaign's question is the DIFFERENCE
# between two of them. exit 2 would be a defect.

unit viper3
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 55.20000 13.52710 5000 90.0 380       # 5.00 nm apart — THE ONE LINE PAIR that differs
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode acm_hud
  set fcr_range_nm 10
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9                            # firing order: the infrared rounds first
  set store 2 aim9
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 3
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 55.20000 14.60000 5000 380               # hulkeast: the MiG's own range target
  objective kill unit fulcrum3
  objective survive

unit fulcrum3
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 55.20000 13.67290 5000 270.0 380
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode acm                           # briefed INTO the fight: the close-combat auto-lock volume
  set n019_range_nm 10
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set kols_mode ir_cc                         # the KOLS in its close-combat field — the third of the
  set kols_laser on                           # quotation's three reasons, and the one o4-08 can blind
  set store 1 r73
  set store 2 r73
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 3
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 55.20000 12.60000 5000 380               # hulkwest: the F-16's own range target
  objective kill unit viper3
  objective survive

unit hulkwest
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 55.20000 12.60000 ground 90.0 0

unit hulkeast
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 55.20000 14.60000 ground 270.0 0
